/**
 * Metro turns `global.css` into a side-effect import that NativeWind consumes
 * (see `metro.config.js` and `global.css`). TypeScript needs to be told the
 * same thing, exactly as it does for `.svg` in `svg.d.ts`.
 *
 * This existed already, by accident. `expo-env.d.ts` references `expo/types`,
 * which carries this declaration -- but that file is generated by the Expo
 * CLI and is gitignored, so it is present on any machine that has run the app
 * and absent on a clean checkout. `npm run typecheck` therefore passed
 * locally and failed in CI with TS2882 on `import '../global.css'`, which is
 * the worst version of a build error: invisible to the person who wrote it.
 *
 * Declaring it here, in a committed file, means the typecheck answers the
 * same way on a laptop and on a runner that has never started Expo.
 */
declare module '*.css';
